{
  "title": "Sesamoid Injuries of the Hallux",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7010/sesamoid-injuries-of-the-hallux",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 29 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sesamoid injuries of the Hallux consist of a constellation of injuries to the sesamoid complex consisting of fractures, tendonitis, and ligamentous injuries.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is suspected with hallux pain that is worse with hyperextension and can be confirmed with MRI studies.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment depends on the specific injury to the sesamoid complex, chronicity and patient activity demands.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Specific injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fracture (caused by hyperextension and axial loading)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dislocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sprain \"**turf toe**\"",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sesamoiditis (trauma or infection)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "chondromalacia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "osteochondritis dissecans",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "FHB tendonitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Tibial sesamoid more commonly injured",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "has greater weight bearing status",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "larger than lateral sesamoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "forced dorsiflexion of first MTP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "potential avulsion of plantar plate off base of phalanx",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "proximal migration of sesamoids",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**bilateral sesamoiditis** should raise alarm and concern for",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**reiter's disease** (urethritis, conjuctivitis / iritis, inflammatory bowel disease)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "psoriatic arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "seronegative RA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sesamoids play important role in function of great toes by",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**absorbing weight-bearing** pressure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "reducing **friction** at MT head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**protect FHL** tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "glides between sesamoids",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "provide **fulcrum** for flexor hallucis brevis that **increases MTP flexion power**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**bipartite sesamoid** present in 10-25%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "97% are in the tibial sesamoid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "25% bilateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Attachments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "FHB attaches to both tibial and fibular sesamoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sesamoids are connected to each other by intersesamoid ligament and plantar plate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "abductor hallucis is connected to tibial sesamoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "adductor hallucis is connected to fibular sesamoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Biomechanics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sesamoid function is analogous to the patella as they increase the mechanical advantage of the FHB",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "generalized big toe pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "worse in terminal part of stance phase",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "possible plantar-flexed MTP with cavus foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of foot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial oblique (sesamoid view)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "axial sesamoid view",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7010/images/Sesamoid%20axial%20view%20illustration_moved.gif",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7010/images/Sesamoid%20axillary%20view%20xray%20-%20Greer%20Richardson_moved.png",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "proximal migration of sesamoids",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "be suspicious of intrinsic minus hallux",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7010/images/Xray%20-%20courtesy%20of%20Richardson_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "helps distinguish a bipartite sesamoid from a fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7010/images/Bone%20scan%20-%20courtesy%20Richardson_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "use caution with interpretation as 25%-30% of asymptomatic patients can have increased uptake",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increased uptake compared to uninjured side helps diagnosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDs, reduced weightbearing, activity modification, orthoses",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indicated as first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "short leg cast with toe extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "acute fracture (controversial)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "shaving keratotic lesion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "keratotic lesion present increasing pressure on sesamoids",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "partial or complete sesamoidectomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "nonoperative management fails after 3-12 months",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique (see below)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "autologous bone grafting",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "nonunion or fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsiflexion osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "plantar-flexed first ray with sesamoid injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Complete or Partial Sesamoidectomy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approaches",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "approach to tibial sesamoid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7010/images/Approach%20to%20tibial%20sesamoid%20-%20courtesy%20Richardson_moved.png",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "medial-plantar approach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "high risk of injuring **proper branch of medial plantar nerve**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "approach to fibular sesamoid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7010/images/Approach%20fibular%20sesamoid%20-%20courtesy%20Richardson_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "plantar approach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "beware for",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "proper branch to lateral side of hallux",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "first common branch to first web space",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**may be partial or complete sesamoidectomy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sesamoid shaving (**contraindicated** in a patient with a plantar flexed 1st MT)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Cock-up deformity**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "removal of both sesamoids is associated with a high incidence of cock-up deformity of the great toe",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "caused by weakening of the flexor hallucis brevis tendon, which should be meticulously repaired after sesamoid excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "excision of both sesamoids should be avoided",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Hallux valgus**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may be caused from tibial sesamoid excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Hallux varus**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may be caused by fibular sesamoid excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
